Kamen Fight - Project DocumentationKamen Fight is a Web-based, turn-based Kamen Rider fighting game built with vanilla JavaScript, HTML5 Video, and CSS3. 
The game features simultaneous command selection, directional charge mechanics, sequential video-driven combat resolution, and full mirror-match support.
Key FeaturesDirectional Charge System: Players hold directional keys (A, D, W, S) to build charge percentage ($10\% - 100\%$) before locking in an attack using command keys (J, K, L, I).
Sequential Video Combat Resolution: Turn resolution plays character video clips in center stage with dynamic overlay banners ([Rider Name] : [Move Name]!).

Action-Over-Idle Turn Priority: Active moves automatically take precedence over DO_NOTHING. Attacks hit idle opponents directly and bypass the defender's idle animation.
4-Hit Faint & Stun System: Landing 4 consecutive hits schedules a faint state for the defender in the following round. Fainted riders loop faint.mp4 during the 5-second countdown, have their controls locked, and auto-execute DO_NOTHING. Hits landed against a fainted target do not stack toward another faint.
Dynamic Floating Damage & Heal Popups: Exact integer damage deals appear as red floating popups (-150) and health recoveries as green popups (+100) directly above the LP bar.

Developer Practice / Dummy Mode: Pressing key 0 at any point during battle toggles Player 2 into constant IDLE mode (DO_NOTHING) for move testing.
Mirror Match & Vertical Scaling Support: Handles duplicate rider matches via horizontal CSS transforms (scaleX(-1)) and hue-rotate color palette swaps. Standardizes 9:16 vertical video assets using object-fit: contain.
Controls & Input MappingInputFunctionDetailsA (Hold)Defense ChargeBase Charge Speed: $800\text{ms}$D (Hold)Offense ChargeBase Charge Speed: $1300\text{ms}$W (Hold)Air / Buff ChargeBase Charge Speed: $2000\text{ms}$S (Hold)Energy / Special ChargeBase Charge Speed: $2600\text{ms}$J, K, L, I
Action KeysPress while holding a direction to confirm moveKey 0Developer ToggleToggles P2 into/out of constant Dummy Idle modeFile & Directory StructurePlaintextKamen_Fight/

├── index.html              # Main game layout and video elements
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # Styling, HUD layout, floating popups, video scaling
├── js/
│   └── game.js             # Core game state, priority logic, video handler, HUD
├── data/
│   └── moves.json          # Move definitions, CHI costs, damage ratios, video mappings
└── assets/
    └── videos/
        └── ichigo/         # Rider video clips (idle.mp4, faint.mp4, hit.mp4, etc.)
Setup & Deployment InstructionsLocal Execution: Clone or download the repository folder and open index.html directly in any modern Web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari). No external dependencies or build steps are required.GitHub Pages Deployment: Push the repository to GitHub and enable GitHub Pages under Settings > Pages.Asset Naming Warning: Ensure all file paths and video filenames inside assets/videos/<rider_id>/ are strictly lowercase (e.g., idle.mp4, faint.mp4) to prevent 404 errors on case-sensitive Linux host servers like GitHub Pages.


